Upstream gap: an OpenAI connection sends all its models through one API, the
one its api_type selects. A gateway that serves Chat Completions models next
to models it reaches natively only through the Responses API, such as
Langflow flows behind LiteLLM, either translates Chat Completions requests for
those models or needs a second connection to the same gateway with a fixed
model_ids allowlist, which hides every model deployed later. Upstream closed
a per-model API type request for this case as not planned:
https://github.com/open-webui/open-webui/issues/22905

Add responses_model_ids to a connection's config in OPENAI_API_CONFIGS: a
list of glob patterns such as ["langflow/*"], matched case-sensitively against
the provider's model IDs before prefix_id applies, as exclude_model_ids is; a
workspace model matches by its base model. Requests for matching models use
the Responses API, as api_type "responses" does for a whole connection; the
connection's other models keep its api_type. Any other value matches no
model, so a mistyped config keeps Chat Completions rather than sending every
model to the Responses API.

Removal check: an Open WebUI release whose Model IDs filter accepts patterns
(https://github.com/open-webui/open-webui/discussions/23711), so a second
connection with api_type "responses" can list the matching models while the
first leaves them out, or one that selects the API type per model.
--- a/open_webui/routers/openai.py
+++ b/open_webui/routers/openai.py
@@ -1525,7 +1525,18 @@

     headers, cookies = await get_headers_and_cookies(request, url, key, api_config, metadata, user=user)

-    is_responses = api_config.get('api_type') == 'responses'
+    from fnmatch import fnmatchcase
+
+    # Patterns match the provider's own model IDs, before prefix_id applies.
+    # Only a list of strings matches; a string would match by its characters.
+    responses_model_ids = api_config.get('responses_model_ids')
+    is_responses = api_config.get('api_type') == 'responses' or (
+        isinstance(responses_model_ids, list)
+        and any(
+            isinstance(pattern, str) and fnmatchcase(str(payload['model']), pattern)
+            for pattern in responses_model_ids
+        )
+    )

